Title: "Overview"
Id: "f9e314a2-4ae8-4b75-aa95-8b5be50b5969"

Text: "Clauses appear in sections such as `satisfies:`, `then:`, `that:`, `where:`,
`when:`, and `suchThat:`.

A clause is one of:

- a **declaration statement** such as `x is \set`
- an **expression** such as `P \.and./ Q`
- a nested **clause group**

The clause groups are:

- `not:`
- `allOf:`
- `anyOf:`
- `oneOf:`
- `equivalently:`
- `exists:` (with optional `suchThat:`)
- `existsUnique:` (with optional `suchThat:`)
- `forAll:` (with optional `where:` and required `then:`)
- `let:` (with optional `where:` and required `then:`)
- `given:` (with optional `where:` and required `then:`)
- `if:` (with `then:`)
- `have:` (with `iff:`)
- `have:` (with `asserting:`, and optional `because:` / `by:`)
- `piecewise:` (with `if:`, `then:`, zero or more `elseIf:`/`then:` pairs,
  and optional `else:`)

A `have:` group containing `iff:` is the biconditional form. Every other
`have:` shape is the proof-style form, whose `asserting:`, `because:`, and `by:`
sections are optional.

Formulation clause entries are tried as declarations first and expressions
second. This lets `x is \set` introduce a type fact in contexts where facts are
assumed.

Bare specifications (`is` and non-predicate infix spec operators `\:...:/`)
introduce symbols, so they are only allowed in binding positions (`exists:`,
`existsUnique:`, `forAll:`, `let:`, `given:` arguments, and
`where:` / `suchThat:` / `when:`). In statement positions (`then:`, `if:`,
`iff:`, `that:`, `else:`, and the boolean combinators) use the predicate forms
`is?` / `is_not?` and `\:...?:/`. See Statements and Specifications.

Each of these clauses also has a builtin command form usable inline in a
statement position — see Builtin Clause Commands.

Quantifier and `let:` declarations are local to the clause group that
introduces them. A nested binding may not shadow a defined symbol from an
inherited scope. Clause bindings use the refined declaration parser, so refined
types are accepted consistently in `given:`, quantifiers, `have:`, and other
binding positions."
Id: "fbc6bc5d-dab9-4c48-b83c-f2aff94640be"
